#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:7
msgid "Generic V4L2 ISP formats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:9
msgid ""
"Generic ISP formats are metadata formats that define a mechanism to pass ISP "
"parameters and statistics between userspace and drivers in V4L2 buffers. "
"They are designed to allow extending them in a backward-compatible way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:14
msgid "ISP parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:16
msgid ""
"The generic ISP configuration parameters format is realized by a defining a "
"single C structure that contains a header, followed by a binary buffer where "
"userspace programs a variable number of ISP configuration data block, one "
"for each supported ISP feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:21
msgid ""
"The :c:type:`v4l2_isp_buffer` structure defines the buffer header which is "
"followed by a binary buffer of ISP configuration data. Userspace shall "
"correctly populate the buffer header with the serialization format version "
"and with the size (in bytes) of the binary data buffer where it will store "
"the ISP blocks configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:27
msgid ""
"Each *ISP configuration block* is preceded by a header implemented by the :c:"
"type:`v4l2_isp_block_header` structure, followed by the configuration "
"parameters for that specific block, defined by the ISP driver specific data "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:32
msgid ""
"Userspace applications are responsible for correctly populating each block's "
"header fields (type, flags and size) and the block-specific parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:36
msgid "ISP parameters block enabling, disabling and configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:38
msgid ""
"When userspace wants to configure and enable an ISP block it shall fully "
"populate the block configuration and set the V4L2_ISP_PARAMS_FL_BLOCK_ENABLE "
"bit in the block header's `flags` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:42
msgid ""
"When userspace simply wants to disable an ISP block the "
"V4L2_ISP_PARAMS_FL_BLOCK_DISABLE bit should be set in block header's `flags` "
"field. Drivers accept a configuration parameters block with no additional "
"data after the header in this case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:47
msgid ""
"If the configuration of an already active ISP block has to be updated, "
"userspace shall fully populate the ISP block parameters and omit setting the "
"V4L2_ISP_PARAMS_FL_BLOCK_ENABLE and V4L2_ISP_PARAMS_FL_BLOCK_DISABLE bits in "
"the header's `flags` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:52
msgid ""
"Setting both the V4L2_ISP_PARAMS_FL_BLOCK_ENABLE and "
"V4L2_ISP_PARAMS_FL_BLOCK_DISABLE bits in the flags field is not allowed and "
"returns an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:56
msgid ""
"Extension to the parameters format can be implemented by adding new blocks "
"definition without invalidating the existing ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:60
msgid "ISP statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:62
msgid ""
"The generic ISP statistics format is identical to the generic ISP "
"configuration parameters format. It is realized by defining a C structure "
"that contains a header, followed by binary buffer where the ISP driver "
"copies a variable number of ISP statistics blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:67
msgid ""
"Extensible statistics buffers have :c:type:`v4l2_isp_buffer` header followed "
"by a binary buffer of ISP statistics data. ISP drivers populate the buffer "
"header with the serialization format version and with the size (in bytes) of "
"the binary data buffer where ISP statistics data are serialized. "
"Applications shall validate that the serialization format version matches "
"the expected one and that the buffer size doesn't exceed the maximum size "
"for a statistics buffer as declared by the driver's uAPI header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:75
msgid ""
"Each *ISP statistics block* is preceded by a header implemented by the :c:"
"type:`v4l2_isp_block_header` structure, followed by the statistics data for "
"that specific block. The driver might optionally report platform-specific "
"flags associated with each statistics block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:80
msgid ""
"Applications inspect the statistics block type as reported in the header and "
"validates the reported size matches the block's expected size before "
"accessing the ISP statistics data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../userspace-api/media/v4l/v4l2-isp.rst:84
msgid ""
"Extension to the statistics format can be implemented by adding new blocks "
"definition without invalidating the existing ones."
msgstr ""

